{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"stop","index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Current and blessed, it penetrates and liberates every situation! Ask the Milder whether it is not so; — she herself, in happy; not Rossini’s music, is this, for her tone, sound, and action are from the house and from the beginning out of passion and soulful penetration, — You yourself also feel this, when in re-echoes or even only in memory this fullness re-echoes in you, lives on, and storms on. — It would still be worth mentioning that finally the first act of yesterday’s ballet was performed; Eberle, a German, danced excellently, though not quite the Italian manner of a Torelli, who with her admirable manners and even more her Roman physiognomy, gave me also an idea of Italian dancing. — But now from these profane observations and plays of the 5th Oct.... The weather has cleared up again this afternoon; certainly the Berliner Dittmar has predicted this, — for here first and in the local newspapers I see how much this prophet here, — where his fatherland is not, — counts; for which reason I also did not stay in Swabia, but went over Nuremberg to Berlin. To return to my dry historical relation, — this morning early to the Imperial and Royal Library, having been with Raphael and Marc Anton. What soulful delicacy, what Unica! Along with this also again a prosaic remark: — here one sees on certain days (in the Imperial and Royal Library every day) all the treasures of artistic genius — free of charge; to the serving attendants one gives perhaps a tip and I have always, even when it was not necessary, given tips, to do honor at least to the royal Prussian professorship. On the other hand, the Berlin-Potsdam dirtiness is notorious here and in the whole world! — and I, royal Professor publ. ordin. at the royal university in Berlin (and indeed Professor of the subject, namely of Philosophy, as the"}}],"created":1795080466,"model":"qwen","system_fingerprint":"b11429-d81235049","object":